me.py`\n   - `/workspace/Python/libraries/recognizers-number-with-unit/recognizers_number_with_unit/resources/spanish_numeric_with_unit.py`\n\n4. **Test Specs** - Added test cases for \"anos\" without tilde:\n   - `/workspace/Specs/NumberWithUnit/Spanish/AgeModel.json` - Added test cases for \"Tengo diez anos\" and \"Mi abuelo tiene ochenta anos\"\n\n### Key Changes:\n\n- **Pattern `a[ñn]o`** matches both \"año\" and \"ano\" (singular)\n- **Pattern `a[ñn]os?`** matches all four forms: \"año\", \"años\", \"ano\", and \"anos\"\n- The `DecadeWithCenturyRegex` now matches decade expressions with both accented and unaccented forms\n- The `AgeSuffixList` and `AmbiguousAgeUnitList` now recognize age expressions with both forms\n- Unit maps now include entries for both \"anos\"/\"ano\" and \"años\"/\"año\"\n\n### Test Results:\n\nThe test script shows that:\n- ✅ Age expressions with \"anos\" (without tilde) are now recognized: \"Tengo diez anos\" → value 10, unit Año\n- ✅ Age expressions with \"anos\" in plural work: \"Mi abuelo tiene ochenta anos\" → value 80, unit Año\n- ✅ Decade expressions are being extracted (though resolution may need parser configuration)\n- ✅ All four forms (año, años, ano, anos) are present in UnitMap and UnitValueMap\n\nThe implementation treats both accented and unaccented forms as equivalent, handling singular and plural forms consistently across all parsing APIs.",
